There are several games that use an affine transform to rotate the main view they're using to display things (probably a `CAEAGLLayer`-backed view). One example is Capcom's Ghosts 'n Goblins (`jp.co.capcom.makaikus`), which doesn't actually work on trunk currently (as of c542a8bfb0787148b23417b8be5852fb3075c676) but with these stubs you can get it to run for long enough to briefly see the rotation:

<details><summary>patch</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_activity_indicator_view.rs b/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_activity_indicator_view.rs
index caaa108..82b7bfe 100644
--- a/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_activity_indicator_view.rs
+++ b/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_activity_indicator_view.rs
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@ pub const CLASSES: ClassExports = objc_classes! {
     // TODO
 }

+- (())setActivityIndicatorViewStyle:(id)_x {}
+
 @end

 };
diff --git a/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view/ui_label.rs b/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view/ui_label.rs
index 44fbcc2..ba371df 100644
--- a/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view/ui_label.rs
+++ b/src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view/ui_label.rs
@@ -118,6 +118,9 @@ pub const CLASSES: ClassExports = objc_classes! {

 // TODO: initWithCoder:

+- (())setShadowColor:(id)_x {}
+- (())setShadowOffset:(id)_x {}
+
 - (id)text {
     env.objc.borrow::<UILabelHostObject>(this).text
 }
```
</details>

For titles like these, you would currently get a 320×320 cropped region of the screen visible, with no rotation, and the bottom 320×160 region of the screen is some background colour.

I've seen screenshots of titles where instead the landscape screen gets stretched (in an aspect-ratio-disrespecting way) into portrait in a similar way. This is presumably a result of the incorrect clipping behaviour that was fixed in 421234fd1f2fd982193d16ba2396ac8fc88a46e9.
